## 7.1 Image Validation

For each image:

1. Identify the exact subject being displayed.
2. Prefer official or authoritative image sources.
3. Check available captions, metadata, identifiers, and source context.
4. Confirm that the photograph relates to the selected subject.
5. Avoid unrelated stock images.
6. Preserve attribution and licensing requirements.
7. Clearly distinguish illustrations from photographs.

When the identity cannot be verified, do not confidently present an unrelated image.

Display an appropriate placeholder or verified alternative instead.

## 7.2 Object-Specific Images

When viewing sculptures, artworks, or museum objects, prefer images of the exact identified object rather than a generic example from the same artistic tradition.

If the system only has an image of a similar object, label it clearly as an example rather than as the actual subject.

## 7.3 Image Performance

Implement:

- Responsive image sizes
- Lazy loading
- Image caching
- Progressive placeholders
- Correct aspect ratios
- Fallback on load failure
- Prevention of layout shifts
- Limits on unnecessary image downloads

Do not sacrifice accuracy to improve loading speed.

